.TH SDE-POWER 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-power \- SDE power manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-power
[\fB\-\-daemon\fR]
.br
.B sde-power \-\-brightness
[\fBget\fR | \fBup\fR | \fBdown\fR | \fIPERCENT\fR]
.br
.B sde-power \-\-profile
[\fBget\fR | \fBlist\fR | \fINAME\fR]
.br
.B sde-power
\fB\-\-status\fR | \fB\-\-osd\fR [\fIPERCENT\fR] | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The power manager of SDE, started with the session through XDG autostart
(\fBsde-power \-\-daemon\fR). It warns about low and critical battery
(UPower) and runs the critical action, handles the lid and the power button
(holding systemd-logind's handle-lid-switch and handle-power-key inhibitors
unless the setting is \fBlogind\fR), dims the screen, turns it off (DPMS)
and suspends after the idle timeouts, separately on battery and AC, unless a
program holds an org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver or logind "idle" inhibitor,
handles the XF86MonBrightnessUp/Down keys with an on-screen display and
switches power-profiles-daemon modes with the power source.
.PP
Settings: \fBsde-settings \-\-page power\fR, or [power] in
~/.config/sde/sde.conf (see /etc/xdg/sde/sde.conf).
.SH D-BUS
org.debion.SDE.Power at /org/debion/SDE/Power on the session bus:
GetBrightness, SetBrightness(i), StepBrightness(i), GetStatus, Reload.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-lock (1),
.BR sde-settings (1)
